nder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting chain from 1006 to 1860 exists in the window under the 600-unit delay bound; the temporal reachable set from 1006 is just itself and 1532. Removing or loosening the delay bound, and widening the window to the full timeline, still yields no arrival at 1860, so the negative is structural/temporal rather than a threshold artifact. The only order-ignoring link runs through the hub 274, whose high degree and the window's large event volume are insufficient evidence of a cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion: no genuine cascade.**\n\nKey findings:\n- Within [32431, 42031], node 1006 has only 2 events (one outgoing, to 1532) and 1860 has 3 events (with 274, 743, 1390) \u2014 disjoint contact sets (step_03, step_06, step_12).\n- Time-respecting search with max_wait=600 reaches only 2 nodes and never arrives at 1860; no paths are enumerated (step_01, step_10).\n- Confounder controls: relaxing the delay constraint entirely (max_wait=null, step_04) and to 3000 (step_11) still fails, so the negative result is not an artifact of the 600-unit gap rule. The static 2-hop/4-hop neighbourhood shows 1006 sits in a tiny component (1075/1532/1036/1643) while 1860 attaches to the high-degree hubs 274/743 (step_05, step_07) \u2014 i.e. an order-ignoring connection exists only through hub 274, whose popularity does not create a valid ordered chain. Extending the window to the whole timeline still yields no time-respecting route (step_13). Overall window volume is high (2090 events, 1422 active nodes; step_02), so the failure is not from sparse sampling of the window, and the endpoints' activity is low and stable across epochs (step_08).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9c9c8a9f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \